# Tracer: exact positive-natural carrier
#
# Before (Litex verified, but compiler emission stopped):
# 1 $in N+
# Former compiler behavior: the verifier recorded the checked closed-numeral
# membership, but the native-carrier compiler had no exact `N+` ABI.
#
# Now: `N+` is the exact subtype of native naturals satisfying `0 < n`.
# Closed positive numerals construct that subtype, and membership projects back
# to `N` without erasing or independently reconstructing the positivity proof.
1 $in N+

forall n N+:
    n $in N

# Boundary (Litex verifies; compiler remains fail-closed):
# 1 $in Q+
# This batch does not generalize one reviewed refined carrier into `Q+` or the
# other sign/nonzero sets; each needs its own exact native predicate contract.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -strict -runner -f lean/examples/20_PositiveNaturalCarrier.lit
# cargo test --release --test litex_to_lean_compiler_tracers positive_natural
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh check examples
